reminds anyone of some persecution.

I'm not a member of a disenfranchised/persecuted/oppressed group (as
far as I know -- any lobbies for bald guys 6'5" or better?), so I can't 
claim to understand the outrage over things like high school mascots.

Take the situation here in Kentucky.  The NAACP has requested that all
high schools (yes, they were contacted individually) using the nickname
